From: bullhead-linux <kaiwalyakhasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:27:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: the shrinker and VRAM carveout objects

Without an IOMMU (msm.allow_vram_carveout) GPU objects come from the VRAM
carveout and have no shmem file. Purging one such object that userspace
marked MSM_MADV_DONTNEED (Mesa's buffer cache) dereferenced obj->filp in
shmem_truncate_range: an oops in kswapd under memory pressure, then in every
task that reclaims, until the phone stops answering. Purge them without the
shmem part (put_pages gives their carveout space back), and never evict
them, as their contents live nowhere else.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c          | 4 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
index eeb3b65dd..e787b6652 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
@@ -870,6 +870,10 @@ void msm_gem_purge(struct drm_gem_object *obj)
 
 	drm_gem_free_mmap_offset(obj);
 
+	/* VRAM carveout objects (no IOMMU) have no shmem file behind them */
+	if (!obj->filp)
+		return;
+
 	/* Our goal here is to return as much of the memory as
 	 * is possible back to the system as we are called from OOM.
 	 * To do this we must instruct the shmfs to drop all of its
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
index 89c0ea8dd..8acf3f307 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
@@ -62,6 +62,10 @@ evict(struct drm_gem_object *obj)
 	if (is_unevictable(to_msm_bo(obj)))
 		return false;
 
+	/* VRAM carveout objects: their contents live nowhere else */
+	if (!obj->filp)
+		return false;
+
 	if (msm_gem_active(obj))
 		return false;
 
-- 
